// A test case is a call too: it passes the function it names (a "cfn" node) to
// the function under test, and a case that names an impure function for a pure
// parameter would run it on a worker thread at build time. So each case's
// arguments are held to the rule ../step.id holds a call's to (E0806, reported at
// the case). A case argument that is not a function name is a literal, which is
// not a function value.

pure_cases(int pq_k) {
  while(pq_k < len((import casenode))) {
    pure_case(pq_k);
    pq_k = pq_k + 1;
  }
} return void;
given pure_fix_cases {
  (0):() then (import chkfail)[0]:(1)
  (1):() then (import chkfail)[0]:(0)
}

